    Fix win-1: box the session futures so debug builds fit Windows' 1 MiB main thread

    Every `blit` run that was a DESTINATION (local copy/mirror/move, pull,
    single-file copy, retry passes) died on Windows with `thread 'main' has
    overflowed its stack`. `#[tokio::main]` polls the command future on the
    process's main thread, Windows gives it 1 MiB, and a debug build's poll
    frames hold every nested future inline. The ssc-6 retry passes inlined a
    second session into every route arm: run_transfer_inner's frame went
    108 KB (ab5ea073) -> 230 KB, run_move_inner's 121 KB -> 243 KB, and the
    real binary's main-thread need on macOS aarch64 rose to 1088-1216 KiB for
    local routes and 1024 KiB for pulls. macOS/Linux give the main thread
    8 MiB, so nothing there could see it.

    Box where one large future nests another, so callers hold a pointer:
    - CLI: main -> run_cli; run_transfer/run_move -> their route dispatch;
      the deferred local/push/pull/delegated wrappers -> their inner run;
      each retry pass in run_retry_passes.
    - blit-core: transfers::local::run -> run_local_session; the local
      session's role join; run_source -> drive_source; run_destination ->
      drive_destination; the push/pull clients -> run_source/run_destination
      and run_remote_push/pull -> the clients; each attempt in
      run_with_retries.
    After the fix every shape needs 496 KiB of main thread on macOS aarch64
    (480 KiB x86_64) — the clap argument-parse floor, not the transfer. No
    stack-size setting is added.

    Guards (both run on every platform):
    - crates/blit-cli/tests/main_thread_stack_budget.rs runs the real binary
      (local copy, mirror + retry pass, move, push, pull, pull mirror, pull +
      retry pass) with its main thread held to 768 KiB on Unix via
      `ulimit -S -s`, natively 1 MiB on Windows. Red on all 7 with the boxing
      reverted (every run overflowed), green with it.
    - crates/blit-core/tests/stack_budget.rs drives a local mirror session
      and a pull-shaped destination session (both carriers) on a 256 KiB
      thread with a current-thread runtime. With the boxing reverted the
      local mirror overflows; the pull shape fits at this layer before and
      after (208/192 KiB -> 160/144 KiB), since the pull regression lived in
      the CLI frames the first guard covers.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

