91e64d88 Fix win-2: a file that enumerates but will not open at scan is listed, not session-fatal
 crates/blit-cli/tests/retry_pass.rs               |  91 ++++++++++++++
 crates/blit-core/src/remote/transfer/source.rs    | 143 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 crates/blit-core/tests/source_side_containment.rs |  65 ++++++++++
 3 files changed, 294 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
commit 91e64d88f999adb5f0c529242f6ab7fcd0239934
Author:     Michael Coelho <mcoelho@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Wed Sep 30 17:52:41 2026 -0400
Commit:     Michael Coelho <mcoelho@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Wed Sep 30 17:52:41 2026 -0400

    Fix win-2: a file that enumerates but will not open at scan is listed, not session-fatal

    On Windows a source file held open with no sharing (NTUSER.DAT, a live
    SQLite database) ended the whole session: `session INTERNAL: manifest
    open …locked.bin: The process cannot access the file because it is being
    used by another process. (os error 32)`. The scan's per-file open check
    recorded PermissionDenied/NotFound as unreadable and turned every other
    error kind — ERROR_SHARING_VIOLATION maps to none — into a session error.

    D-2026-09-28-2 (no one error is fatal to the run) and D-2026-09-28-4
    (mirror safety rests on enumeration completeness; a file in the manifest
    is never extraneous): any other open error now lists the file. Its header
    goes on the manifest, the scan stays complete, and the payload path
    reports it per file (`source: cannot open: …`) if it still cannot be read
    — which also puts it in the retry passes' set and keeps its destination
    counterpart under mirror. PermissionDenied/NotFound at scan are unchanged
    (owner-pinned; whether PermissionDenied should also become per-file is
    recorded as an open owner question in the plan).

    The scan's Windows-metadata read (GetFileAttributesW + stream
    enumeration) does not need data access and succeeds on the held file
    (proven on the VM: the mirror guard below completes with the scan
    complete and Windows metadata preserved), so it needed no change.

    Guards:
    - source.rs scan_open_tests (portable): the scan with an injected
      sharing-violation-shaped open error lists both files and records
      nothing unreadable; a PermissionDenied is still an unreadable entry.
      Red with the old arm restored (`manifest open …`), green with the fix.
    - source_side_containment windows_sharing_violation_is_skipped_and_reported
      (existing) and the new windows_sharing_violation_under_mirror_keeps_the_counterpart
      (both carriers; counterpart kept, extraneous entry deleted).
    - retry_pass windows_a_locked_source_file_is_retried_and_its_counterpart_kept:
      the real CLI with the file held — reported once, `(retried)`, exit 2,
      counterpart kept; freed during the wait, it lands on the retry, exit 0.
      The three Windows guards are red on the Windows 11 ARM64 VM with the old
      arm restored and green with the fix.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

