    Fix win-4: a copy or mirror push compares with the copy rule again

    Since ssc-6 every `blit copy`/`blit mirror` PUSH re-sent every file on
    every platform. ssc-6 routed the copy/mirror push

[ptk output] action=read state=available complete=true bytes=44981 provenance=powershell_objects offset=30000 next_offset=44981 bytes_returned=14981
 through
    run_remote_push_transfer_deferred so the retry passes can run before the
    one final summary; that wrapper had been move's alone and hard-coded
    `move_verb: true`, so the push compared with the move mapping
    (IgnoreTimes: transfer unconditionally) instead of size + mtime. The pull
    and delegated deferred wrappers already take `move_verb`.

    Only Windows noticed: windows_metadata.rs:246 (remote) expects the default
    compare to leave an erased named stream erased on a size/mtime-matched
    file, and the unconditional re-send restored it. It passes at ab5ea073 on
    the Windows 11 ARM64 VM (baseline clone) and failed at 5eeff4ac, so it is
    a regression, not the VM. A temporary diagnostic on the VM showed the
    daemon diffing the second push as Modified with size and mtime equal to
    the header's.

    The deferred push takes `move_verb` like its pull sibling: copy/mirror
    (main pass and retry pass) pass false, move passes true — the move rule
    stays pinned by remote_move's move_lands_source_bytes_over_same_size_newer_destination.

    Guard (portable): remote_transfer_edges
    a_second_push_of_an_unchanged_tree_transfers_nothing — copy and mirror
    push the same tree twice; the second transfers 0 files. Red on macOS
    with the fix reverted (3 files re-sent), green with it; green on the VM,
    where windows_metadata (both tests) now passes too.

